                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "A very short game, but one with a really strong and emotional message. I think people who have struggled with depression themselves might find it easier to connect with what the game is trying to portray. The different tasks might seem simple at first, like having to go to the bathroom, but even something that basic can feel like a real challenge when you're struggling mentally.\n\nThe metaphors, especially the men trapped in the cage and the obsession with the pictures, were fantastic. In such a short amount of time, the game manages to portray different aspects of mental illness, like schizophrenia, paranoia, hallucinations and a lack of motivation. I also really liked how even the simplest objectives become a challenge, showing how much depression can affect everyday life. And in the end, it leaves you with a reality that feels painfully real for many people who struggle with their mental health.",
